10#,#10 Major#,#Chemical Engineering#,#Bachelor of Science in Chemical Engineering

This degree is intended for the student who seeks a broad education in the application of chemical engineering to a variety of specific areas, including energy and the environment, nanotechnology, polymers and colloids, surface science, catalysis and reaction engineering, systems and process design, and biotechnology. The degree requirements include the core chemical engineering subjects with a chemistry emphasis, and the opportunity to add subjects in any of these application areas.

foundational_subjects
intermediate_subjects
advanced_subjects
restricted_electives
communication

%% Foundational subjects required for all ChemE majors
foundational_subjects, "Foundational Subjects" := 5.12, 5.310, 5.601, 10.10, (18.03/18.032)

%% Intermediate core subjects
intermediate_subjects, "Intermediate Subjects" := (5.03/5.07/5.13/(5.611,5.612)/7.05), (10.26/10.27/10.28/10.29/10.467), 10.213, 10.301, 10.302

%% Advanced core subjects - must complete 4 of 5
advanced_subjects, "Advanced Subjects" := (10.492A/10.492B/10.493/10.494A/10.494B){>=2}, 10.32, 10.37, 10.490

